# Twyne voice repair — 6 November 2026

Prepared locally; production deployment awaits confirmation.

## Findings

The earlier speech-dispatch patch remains absent from the live provider function metadata. Production Twyne deployment `61539c46-0ead-421e-adcc-bb0287ececa1` runs commit `c4362b1129aa76e33bea9741f214a41927a78c52`, predating the readable-error commit `7a7c68ba`.

The exact incident `b80a3e60-37fc-4cb3-976c-a31e219f164d` was not found in bounded Convex and gateway runtime logs, or Twyne PostHog exception lookups for 30 October–6 November. The missing earlier fix is confirmed; correlation of that exact reference remains unconfirmed.

## Changes

- Restore the earlier provider speech allowlist fix while retaining ownership, product, session and duplicate-dispatch checks.
- Use Twyne’s paper-and-ink voice menu, opening above the player, with keyboard navigation, typeahead, focus return, Escape, Tab and exact selected-value display.
- Carry safe HTTP status/provider/operation evidence through client error normalization. Credit failures point to Add credit; hosted route failures do not direct users to repair personal settings; real sign-in failures retain sign-in recovery.
- Give hosted transport timeouts a support reference and retry action. Preserve the earlier full error panel, copyable reference, retry and skip behavior.

## Validation

- 102 Twyne speech/error tests; 3 provider dispatch tests.
- Twyne TypeScript and focused ESLint pass.
- Client and server builds pass for the isolated release snapshot.
- Browser: pointer, arrows, Home/End, typeahead, Escape, Tab, upward placement and 320px viewport pass, no page errors.
- Both production Convex dry-runs pass; no index deletions. Twyne CLI pinned to the existing 1.46.0 function runtime.
- Provider full-repository TypeScript check hits an existing missing `dts-bundle-generator` dependency in `packages/sdk/build.ts`; its Convex deployment typecheck passes.
- No paid live narration request was made. Playback is not yet verified in production.

## Prepared releases

Twyne: `/tmp/twyne-voice-release-20261106`, based on its currently deployed frontend commit plus only the voice repair files.
Provider: `/tmp/provider-voice-release-20261106`, preserving `/tmp/notorganic-account-sync-release-20261106` backend sources and its already-deployed chat sync, with only `convex/asyncMedia.ts` overlaid for speech.

